---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import AnchorHeading from '@astrojs/starlight/components/AnchorHeading.astro';
import { SOURCE_AVAILABLE_FROM_VER } from '@data/versions';
---

<LegalLayout
	title="ThingsBoard Community Edition vs Professional Edition: What's the Difference"
	description="Compare ThingsBoard Community Edition and Professional Edition features, deployment options, and migration path."
>
	<div class="markdown-body">

		<div class="site-name"><a href="/">ThingsBoard</a></div>

		<div class="busl-banner">
			<p class="busl-banner__title">
				From version {SOURCE_AVAILABLE_FROM_VER}, ThingsBoard becomes a source-available product
			</p>
			<p class="busl-banner__text">Keep what you run today free with the Community Grant Program.</p>
			<a class="busl-banner__cta print:hidden" href="/community-grant-program/">
				Full guide for Community Edition Users <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
			</a>
		</div>

		<h1>ThingsBoard Community Edition vs Professional Edition: What's the Difference</h1>

		<AnchorHeading level={2} id="unlocking-iot-potential-with-thingsboard">Unlocking IoT Potential with ThingsBoard</AnchorHeading>
		<p>ThingsBoard was originally created to help organizations worldwide unlock the full potential of IoT.
			Established with a vision to simplify and speed up IoT adoption, our mission is to make this
			technology accessible, scalable, and flexible for organizations of all sizes. We empower businesses
			to optimize operations, reduce costs, and discover new opportunities using cutting-edge tools.</p>
		<p>To achieve this, we offer two powerful editions of our platform: Community Edition (CE) and
			Professional Edition (PE). Whether you start with the CE or the advanced features of PE,
			ThingsBoard provides a clear path to build, launch, and scale your IoT solution.</p>

		<AnchorHeading level={2} id="thingsboard-community-edition-ce-the-source-available-powerhouse">ThingsBoard Community Edition (CE): The Source-Available Powerhouse</AnchorHeading>
		<p>ThingsBoard CE is the most feature-rich source-available IoT platform in the world, and we are
			committed to keeping it that way. It is a fully-functional, scalable, and fault-tolerant solution
			that can be deployed in a cluster and used in commercial projects. CE provides a robust foundation
			for building anything from a small proof-of-concept to a large-scale IoT solution.</p>
		<p>⚙️ <strong>CE Features:</strong></p>
		<ul>
			<li><em>Standard Protocol Support</em>: Connect devices via MQTT, CoAP, HTTP, SNMP, and LWM2M.</li>
			<li><em>IoT Gateway</em>: Integrate industrial systems with built-in connectors (Modbus, OPC-UA, BACnet, etc).</li>
			<li><em>Device &amp; Asset Management</em>: Model your physical environment with digital twins.</li>
			<li><em>Data Processing &amp; Alarms</em>: Process data, create alarms, and trigger actions with the rule engine and calculated fields.</li>
			<li><em>Data Visualization</em>: Use real-time, interactive dashboards to visualize telemetry data.</li>
			<li><em>High Scalability</em>: A fault-tolerant clustering architecture supports millions of devices.</li>
		</ul>
		<p class="print:hidden">📌 Learn more: <a href="/docs/">Community Edition</a></p>

		<AnchorHeading level={2} id="thingsboard-professional-edition-pe-enterprise-grade-features-support">ThingsBoard Professional Edition (PE): Enterprise-Grade Features &amp; Support</AnchorHeading>
		<p>ThingsBoard PE is built for enterprises and businesses that want to reduce time-to-market, cut
			development costs, and access more features out-of-the-box. Including all the powerful features of
			the Community Edition, we believe PE is the most feature-rich commercial IoT platform available.
			Our development model reflects our commitment to the community, with 80% of our code
			changes contributed directly to CE, while PE receives additional enterprise-focused features and
			dedicated support.</p>
		<p>🚀 <strong>PE Features:</strong></p>
		<ul>
			<li><em>Everything from CE</em>.</li>
			<li><em>Advanced Access Control (RBAC)</em>: Define custom user roles with granular permissions for devices, assets, and dashboards.</li>
			<li><em>White-Labeling</em>: Customize the platform with your own branding.</li>
			<li><em>Platform Integrations</em>: Connect seamlessly with cloud services like AWS IoT and Azure IoT Hub, plus Kafka and LoRaWAN network servers.</li>
			<li><em>Device Library</em>: Simplify LoRaWAN and other device onboarding with over 400 pre-built data converters.</li>
			<li><em>Automated Reporting</em>: Generate and distribute scheduled reports to customers automatically.</li>
			<li><em>Solution Templates</em>: Accelerate development with pre-built, ready-to-use IoT solution templates.</li>
			<li><em>Support &amp; SLA</em>: Get dedicated support and an uptime SLA on our managed cloud offerings.</li>
		</ul>
		<p class="print:hidden">📌 Learn more: <a href="/docs/pe/">Professional Edition</a></p>

		<hr />

		<AnchorHeading level={2} id="feature-comparison">Feature Comparison</AnchorHeading>
		{/* The table scrolls in this wrapper rather than being display:block itself,
		    which would strip its table role. */}
		<div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-labelledby="feature-comparison-caption" tabindex="0" data-scroll-region>
			<table>
				{/* Hidden: the <h2> above already shows this text. */}
				<caption id="feature-comparison-caption" class="table-caption print:hidden"
					>ThingsBoard Community Edition compared with Professional Edition: feature comparison</caption
				>
				<thead>
					<tr>
						<th scope="col">Feature Category</th>
						<th scope="col">Feature</th>
						<th scope="col">Community Edition</th>
						<th scope="col">Professional Edition</th>
					</tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody>
					<tr>
						<th rowspan="6">Platform Core</th>
						<th scope="row">Multi-Tenancy</th>
						<td>Yes</td>
						<td>Yes</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Scalability (Clustering)</th>
						<td>Yes</td>
						<td>Yes</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Rule Engine &amp; Data Processing</th>
						<td>Yes</td>
						<td>Yes</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">AI Models and AI Rule nodes</th>
						<td>Yes</td>
						<td>Yes</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">End-user real-time dashboards</th>
						<td>Yes</td>
						<td>Yes</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Mobile Application</th>
						<td>Yes</td>
						<td>Yes</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th rowspan="4">Device Management</th>
						<th scope="row">Device &amp; Asset Modeling</th>
						<td>Yes</td>
						<td>Yes</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Device Claiming &amp; Provisioning API</th>
						<td>Yes</td>
						<td>Yes</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Bulk Device and Asset Provisioning via CSV</th>
						<td>Yes</td>
						<td>Yes</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">OTA Updates</th>
						<td>Yes</td>
						<td>Yes</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th rowspan="4">Connectivity</th>
						<th scope="row">Standard IoT Protocols (MQTT/CoAP/HTTP/SNMP/LWM2M)</th>
						<td>Yes</td>
						<td>Yes</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Industrial IoT Gateway (Modbus, OPC-UA, BACnet, etc.)</th>
						<td>Yes</td>
						<td>Yes</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">LPWAN Integrations (LoRaWAN, Sigfox)</th>
						<td>No</td>
						<td>Yes</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">System Integrations (AWS IoT, Azure IoT, PubSub, Kafka)</th>
						<td>No</td>
						<td>Yes</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th rowspan="5">Security &amp; Admin</th>
						<th scope="row">User Management</th>
						<td>Yes</td>
						<td>Yes</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Audit Logging</th>
						<td>Yes</td>
						<td>Yes</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Advanced Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)</th>
						<td>No</td>
						<td>Yes</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Single Sign-On (SSO) / OAuth2</th>
						<td>No</td>
						<td>Yes</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Secrets Storage</th>
						<td>No</td>
						<td>Yes</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th rowspan="4">Go-to-Market</th>
						<th scope="row">White-Labeling</th>
						<td>No</td>
						<td>Yes</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Reporting &amp; Scheduling</th>
						<td>No</td>
						<td>Yes</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Solution Templates</th>
						<td>No</td>
						<td>Yes</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Device Payload Codec Library (400+)</th>
						<td>No</td>
						<td>Yes</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th rowspan="3">Deployment Options</th>
						<th scope="row">Self-Managed (On-premise/Cloud)</th>
						<td>Yes</td>
						<td>Yes</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Managed ThingsBoard Cloud</th>
						<td>No</td>
						<td>Yes</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Managed Private Cloud</th>
						<td>No</td>
						<td>Yes</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th>Support</th>
						<th scope="row">Support Model</th>
						<td>Community</td>
						<td>Advanced + response targets</td>
					</tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>

		<hr />

		<AnchorHeading level={2} id="migration-from-ce-to-pe">Migration From CE to PE</AnchorHeading>
		<p>One of the most powerful advantages of the ThingsBoard ecosystem is the <strong>seamless migration
			path from CE to PE</strong>. You can start your project on CE to prove its value, and when your
			business is ready to scale, you can upgrade to PE without changing your core platform.</p>
		<p>This reduces both technological and business risks, accelerates time-to-market, and enables
			building IoT solutions with a focus on <strong>growth</strong>.</p>

		<hr />

		<AnchorHeading level={2} id="how-to-start-using-thingsboard-ce-and-pe">How to start using ThingsBoard CE and PE</AnchorHeading>
		<p>Choosing the right edition is only half the job. It's equally important to select the
			<strong>right model</strong> to match your goals, resources, and infrastructure strategy.</p>

		<AnchorHeading level={3} id="getting-started-with-community-edition">✅ Getting started with Community Edition</AnchorHeading>
		<ol>
			<li>
				<strong>Self-managed (On-premise)</strong><br />
				Full control in your own or isolated data centers, or offline/on-premise setups.<br />
				<span class="print:hidden">🔗 <a href="/docs/installation/">Self-managed</a></span>
			</li>
		</ol>

		<hr />

		<AnchorHeading level={3} id="getting-started-with-professional-edition">🚀 Getting started with Professional Edition</AnchorHeading>
		<p>Depending on your control, responsibility, and time-to-market requirements, ThingsBoard PE offers
			multiple deployment paths:</p>
		<ol>
			<li>
				<strong>ThingsBoard Cloud (Europe &amp; North America)</strong><br />
				The fastest way to start. Managed by the ThingsBoard team — just connect your devices and
				start.<br />
				<span class="print:hidden">🔗 <a href="/installations/">ThingsBoard Cloud</a></span>
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>ThingsBoard Private Cloud (EU, US, APAC)</strong><br />
				A dedicated and fully managed cluster with an uptime SLA. Ideal for scaling to hundreds of
				thousands or millions of devices.<br />
				<span class="print:hidden">🔗 <a href="/pricing/?product=thingsboard-private-cloud">Private Cloud</a></span>
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Self-managed (On-premise PE)</strong><br />
				Full control in your own data centers. ThingsBoard provides remote support for self-managed
				installations.<br />
				<span class="print:hidden">🔗 <a href="/pricing/?product=thingsboard-pe&solution=pe-pay-as-you-go">Self-managed</a></span>
			</li>
		</ol>

		<div class="footer border-top border-gray-light mt-5 pt-3 text-right text-gray print:hidden">
			This site is open source. <a href="https://github.com/thingsboard/thingsboard.io/edit/main/src/pages/ce-vs-pe-diff/index.astro">Improve this page</a>.
		</div>

	</div>

	{/* Inside the layout: content placed after </LegalLayout> is emitted after </html>. */}
	<script>
		import { initAnchorCopy } from '@util/anchor-copy';
		import { initScrollRegions } from '@util/scroll-regions';
		initScrollRegions();
		initAnchorCopy();
	</script>
</LegalLayout>

<style lang="scss">
	@use '../../styles/_variables.scss' as v;

	// Reset LegalLayout's .legal-page container styles
	// !important needed because our :global rules are injected before LegalLayout's styles
	:global(.legal-page) {
		max-width: unset !important;
		padding: 0 !important;
		font-family: unset !important;
		font-size: unset !important;
		line-height: unset !important;
		text-align: unset !important;
		color: unset !important;
	}

	// Scoped styles — Astro adds [data-astro-cid-*] to all elements below,
	// giving higher specificity than LegalLayout's global styles.
	// For LegalLayout's !important rules (ul, li), we also use !important.
	.busl-banner {
		margin-bottom: 24px;
		padding: 16px 20px;
		border: 1px solid #f0d58c;
		border-left: 4px solid #d4a72c;
		border-radius: 6px;
		background-color: #fff8e5;

		&__title {
			margin: 0 0 4px;
			font-size: 1.25em;
			font-weight: 600;
			color: #24292e;
		}

		&__text {
			margin: 0 0 12px;
			color: #24292e;
		}
	}

	// Written as .markdown-body descendants so they out-rank the generic
	// `.markdown-body a` / `a:hover` link styling further down.
	.markdown-body .busl-banner__cta {
		display: inline-block;
		padding: 8px 16px;
		border-radius: 6px;
		background-color: #0366d6;
		color: #fff;
		font-weight: 600;
		text-decoration: none;

		&:hover {
			background-color: #0256b9;
			text-decoration: none;
		}
	}

	.markdown-body {
		font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif,
			'Apple Color Emoji', 'Segoe UI Emoji', 'Segoe UI Symbol';
		font-size: 16px;
		line-height: 1.5;
		word-wrap: break-word;
		color: #24292e;
		max-width: 980px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 45px;

		a {
			color: #0366d6;
			text-decoration: none;

			&:hover {
				text-decoration: underline;
			}
		}

		p,
		ol,
		table,
		pre {
			margin-top: 0;
			margin-bottom: 16px;
		}

		ul {
			margin-top: 0 !important;
			margin-bottom: 16px !important;
			padding-left: 2em !important;
			list-style: disc !important;
		}

		ul li {
			color: #24292e !important;
			list-style: disc !important;
			margin-bottom: 0 !important;
		}

		li + li {
			margin-top: 0.25em;
		}

		ol {
			padding-left: 2em;
		}

		hr {
			height: 0.25em;
			padding: 0;
			margin: 24px 0;
			background-color: #e1e4e8;
			border: 0;
		}

		h1,
		h2,
		h3,
		h4,
		h5,
		h6 {
			margin-top: 24px;
			margin-bottom: 16px;
			font-weight: 600;
			line-height: 1.25;
		}

		.site-name {
			padding-bottom: 0.3em;
			font-size: 2em;
			font-weight: 600;
			line-height: 1.25;
			border-bottom: 1px solid #eaecef;
			margin-top: 0;
			margin-bottom: 16px;
			text-align: left;
		}

		h1 {
			padding-bottom: 0.3em;
			font-size: 2em;
			border-bottom: 1px solid #eaecef;
			text-align: left !important;
		}

		h2 {
			padding-bottom: 0.3em;
			font-size: 1.5em;
			border-bottom: 1px solid #eaecef;
		}

		h3 {
			font-size: 1.25em;
		}

		h4 {
			font-size: 1em;
		}

		// Horizontal scroll lives on the wrapper, so the table keeps its role.
		.table-scroll {
			overflow-x: auto;
			margin-bottom: 16px;

			// The p/ol/table/pre rule above gives every table a 16px bottom margin;
			// the wrapper is a block formatting context, so that margin cannot
			// collapse out of it and the gap below the card would double.
			table {
				margin-bottom: 0;
			}
		}

		.table-caption {
			@include v.caption-hidden;
		}

		table {
			width: 100%;
			border-spacing: 0;
			border-collapse: collapse;

			thead th {
				font-weight: 600;
			}

			// The category and feature cells are <th> now; they read as body text.
			tbody th {
				font-weight: 400;
				text-align: start;
			}

			th,
			td {
				padding: 6px 13px;
				border: 1px solid #dfe2e5;
			}

			tr {
				background-color: #fff;
				border-top: 1px solid #c6cbd1;

				&:nth-child(2n) {
					background-color: #f6f8fa;
				}
			}
		}

		strong {
			font-weight: 600;
		}

		@media screen and (max-width: 767px) {
			padding: 15px;
		}

		@media print {
			padding: 0;

			tbody tr:not(:has(+ tr > th[rowspan])) {
				break-after: avoid;
			}

			table :is(th, td) {
				padding: 4px 8px;
			}

			thead th:nth-child(2) {
				width: 42%;
			}

			tbody th[scope='row'] {
				overflow-wrap: anywhere;
			}

			.busl-banner__text {
				margin-bottom: 0;
			}
		}
	}

	.border-top { border-top: 1px #e1e4e8 solid !important; }
	.border-gray-light { border-color: #eaecef !important; }
	.text-gray { color: #586069 !important; }
	.mt-5 { margin-top: 32px !important; }
	.pt-3 { padding-top: 16px !important; }
	.text-right { text-align: right !important; }

	// Section headings come from Starlight's AnchorHeading, outside this file's scope, and
	// Starlight's own anchor styles only apply inside `.sl-markdown-content`.
	.markdown-body :global(.sl-heading-wrapper) {
		margin-top: 24px;
		margin-bottom: 16px;
		font-weight: 600;
		line-height: 1.25;

		&:global(.level-h2) {
			padding-bottom: 0.3em;
			font-size: 1.5em;
			border-bottom: 1px solid #eaecef;
		}

		&:global(.level-h3) {
			font-size: 1.25em;
		}

		:global(:is(h2, h3)) {
			display: inline;
			margin: 0;
			font-size: inherit;
			font-weight: inherit;
			line-height: inherit;
		}
	}

	.markdown-body :global(.sl-anchor-link) {
		margin-inline-start: 0.25em;
		color: #0366d6;

		:global(svg) {
			width: 0.8em;
			height: 0.8em;
			vertical-align: middle;
		}

		// No Starlight utility CSS on this layout to hide the link's accessible label.
		:global(.sr-only) {
			position: absolute;
			width: 1px;
			height: 1px;
			overflow: hidden;
			clip-path: inset(50%);
			white-space: nowrap;
		}

		@media (hover: hover) {
			opacity: 0;
		}
	}

	.markdown-body :global(.sl-heading-wrapper:hover .sl-anchor-link),
	.markdown-body :global(.sl-anchor-link:focus-visible) {
		opacity: 1;
	}
</style>
